eel about the game but  this just isn't the case for most people  have sent over there arrived the night  before and we're back on the plane by  the end of the day after the event it's  not like they were sent on a two-week  holiday it was very well structured and  there was limited time to do anything  outside of the proposed timetable that  we're all sent beforehand especially for  those of us that weren't transit over 30  hours one way to make it to the event in  this video I'll be talking about my  experience on this trip covering the  wider timetable behind this event and my  thoughts and feelings based on what was  presented to us in the following videos  that I'll release over the next day or  so are going to further detail on the  PvP gameplay and skills that were played  and tested out the general timetable  went something like this  I think I probably had the furthest way  to come so my flights were a little more  complicated to organize for this reason  I actually ended up in Sweden a good day  and a half before everyone else for  example my trip on the way to the venue  had me catching a plane from Auckland at  New Zealand from 4 p.m. flying for 18  hours  arriving in Doha hanging around there  for a couple of hours catching another  seven hour flight to Stockholm so I was  finally in Sweden but I had a couple of  hours of hanging around to catch my last  1 hour flight to Malmo god I wish I  could sleep on planes  [Music]  anyway I eventually made it to my hotel  which happened to be a two minute walk  away from massive studios at this stage  I had a couple of days to burn before  the event I won't bore you with the  details but summing up Sweden is a  beautiful country they'll definitely be  back someday to do some more exploring  on December 13th all of the youtubers  streamers and other social media  influences met up in the reception area  at massive we were then herded into a  side meeting room when they gave us an  up-to-date overview of the divisi