rd to it  unfortunately I can't give you too much  info on this right now all we know right  now is that has been set up for waiters  to quickly be able to find people to  play with it's sort of like an  extensions of a friends list that's  super easy and quick to navigate  on top of us there will be some some  unclaimed ranking or challenge system  that will allow the more active and  competitive members of the clan to strut  the stuff I'm definitely looking forward  to finding out more information on us we  have a pretty awesome discord channel  but I see this is an in-game extension  to it no idea on Clan numbers at the  stage and whether an inter clan  competitive system will be implemented  but the way they've set it up does give  the feel that they'll be keeping things  quite open to allow for easy additions  later on after the presentation we were  then shuffled to the other side of the  massive building pun intended we will be  split into teams of four in separate  into different rooms each rig was set up  ready first to start straightaway one  thing to note is that we were on  consoles Xboxes and I'll be the first to  admit that after 12 months on PC I'm a  little rusty on controller here is very  shamelessly name-drop who was teamed up  with in a squad there's a couple of  spanish players who are having a few  issues with understanding me not that  surprising really there are a number of  english-speaking countries that struggle  to understand what I'm trying to say but  also in the room was Marco style and a  lot of my earlier videos I reference  Marco as most of them were about  simplifying some of the more intricate  details of the game it's more easily  digestible format for beginners and  people new to the RPG genre but don't  worry guys as much as I was fangirling  out at this whole situation awesome I  totally played it cool  long story short Marco and I are totally  BFFs now hello  it's me the first thing I noticed about  the game is that it was be